# A ball times a number a of the format, with a one-limb center: the center by one operation of T, the radius in the second design.
# The radius is evaluated by operations rounded to nearest on nonnegative values and inflated
# once (milestone1.md, "The radius, second design"): E turns the error bound of the center
# kernel mul_1_1 into a multiple of |cz0|, G covers the roundings of the radius, H what underflow
# loses and the absolute term of the bound. Each is an exact expression rounded up.
kernel:        ball_scale_1
input:         stored cx
input:         stored rx
input:         a
output:        cz
output:        rz
value:         cx*a
requires:      nonneg rx
ensures:       encloses cz rz x*a x=cx,rx
min_precision: 1
theorem:       proofs/theories/Ball2.v ball_scale_1_correct
source:        midpoint-radius scaling (Milestone 1 listing, second radius design)
license:       algorithm and proof: MIT
status:        proved
entry:         yes
cone_exempt:   the radius never reaches the center; the special states of the ball layer (Milestone 1 statements, Ball kernels) test the center and the radii

cz = prod(cx, a)
aa = abs(a)
az = abs(cz)
p  = prod(aa, rx)
t  = fma(az, const up(unit(mul_1_1)/(1-unit(mul_1_1))), p)
rz = fma(t, const up((1+u)^3), const up((1+u)*((1+u)^2*eta+tiny(mul_1_1)/(1-unit(mul_1_1))+eta/2)))
